nodecode-gateway-guardian is a rewrite of kawsthingz's kawsthingz/kawsthingz-hermes-gateway-guardian:

  https://github.com/kawsthingz/kawsthingz-hermes-gateway-guardian
  commit f9959e4b1006ced16d1c6d6647dabe7c99f5aeb1

MIT — declared in that repository's plugin.yaml, which carries no LICENSE file —
Copyright (c) 2026 kawsthingz (plugin.yaml)

What was rewritten: the plugin's two tools and its slash command are this
cell's two tools and `/gateway-guardian`; its pattern counts, its OK/DEGRADED/
BLOCKED thresholds, its cause sentences, its recovery checklists and its
append-only intent log are the same logic, written again in Common Lisp against
the Nodecode cell contract. Its regular expressions became the literal phrases
those expressions named, since the core carries no regular expressions; a line
is still counted once per phrase it carries. Its declared tools, hooks and
command names are unchanged in spirit, prefixed as Nodecode names tools.

What was left out and why: the plugin was written for one agent runtime — it
resolved that runtime's home from an environment variable, walked its profile
folders for logs, and recognised its gateway processes by their command line.
This cell reads the log files its section names (defaulting to the newest under
this home) and recognises this runtime's own gateway process by /proc, so it
answers for the gateway it runs beside. Nothing was added: no network call, no
credential, no telemetry.
